Here are the two commands you need, from your acdt_camry folder:


To bring everything UP (after a reboot or downtime)

```bash
cd ~/Desktop/acdt_camry
source .venv/bin/activate
sudo docker compose up -d
sudo fuser -k 8501/tcp && sleep 1 && python main.py
```

- The first line starts all the databases, broker, Ditto, etc.  
- The second line launches the simulator, data pipeline, predictive model, Ditto sync, rule engine, and the Agent Chat UI at **http://localhost:8501**.



To bring everything DOWN (and release RAM)

```bash
# In the terminal running python main.py → press Ctrl+C
# Then:
sudo docker compose down
```

That’s it — your laptop goes back to normal. Nothing restarts automatically on reboot.



AUTONOMOUS:
System monitors continuously → Detects issue → 
Acts on its own → Notifies mechanic → Logs decision


To make it autonomous you need 3 things:
1. Autonomous Monitor Loop
Runs every X seconds, checks sensors, and triggers agents automatically without user input — no question needed.
2. Action Engine
When an agent detects a critical condition, it doesn't just report it — it acts: sends alerts, logs decisions, schedules appointments, escalates to mechanic.
3. Mechanic Digital Twin Interface
A separate Ditto Thing representing the mechanic that receives emergency packets from the vehicle twin — structured data a mechanic dashboard can read.


Autonomous Monitor (every 30s)
         │
         ├── Safety Agent checks sensors
         │       │
         │       ├── SAFE → log, continue
         │       ├── WARNING → alert driver, log event
         │       └── CRITICAL → trigger Action Engine
         │                         │
         │                         ├── Push to Mechanic Twin (Ditto)
         │                         ├── Log emergency packet (MongoDB)
         │                         └── Cache alert (Redis)
         │
         └── Preventive Agent checks schedule
                 │
                 ├── OK → continue
                 └── OVERDUE → notify driver, push to mechanic twin


So the UI becomes essentially a smart chat companion — like having a co-pilot that speaks first when something needs attention, and listens when the driver wants to talk.

## ACDT v3 — Final Vision

**The Core Idea**
The car has a co-pilot. It talks to the driver like a person — proactively when something needs attention, and responsively when the driver asks. The driver sees a clean chat interface, nothing technical. The AI handles everything in the background.

---

**The Chat Experience**
```
